    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> be two non-zero vectors&nbsp;perpendicular to each other and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>|</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>|</mo></math>, If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>|</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>|</mo></math>,&nbsp;then the angle between the vectors<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is equal to :",
